    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0147" n="131" xml:id="pg131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890.0145/5–2549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Iran
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d40-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-24T19:00:00-04:00">May 24, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                </p>
                <p>474. [Here follow two paragraphs concerning a broadcast on May 20 by Radio Tehran
                    which gave the text of Iranian legislation dealing with subsea resources, along
                    the lines of telegram 691 from Tehran, <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Dept believes Iran action, if verified by you, makes it imperative Emb approach
                    Iran Gov earliest with view achieving purpose set for Para 2 Jidda’s [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dhahran’s</hi>] 165, May 14<anchor n="2" xml:id="d40-f2"
                    /> (to Tehran as 58). Conversation wld be based on Dept’s A–23, Mar 2 and
                    subsequent communications setting forth desirable principles.</p>
                <p>Dept is concerned lest ambiguous wording Iran bill (such as “riches in the sea”
                    which cld be interpreted as not referring to minerals under the sea but
                    including fish) set undesirable precedent in regard to both tone and
                    content.</p>
                <p>You shld inform Brit Amb this instr and discuss desirability Brit following
                    action in light Emb London’s 2006, May 23<anchor n="3" xml:id="d40-f3"/> (to
                    Tehran as 61). Emb London shld inform Brit Govt Dept believes impending Iran
                    action makes immediate approach necessary.</p>
                <p>Dept hopes you can influence Iran Gov to amend bill to set forth clearly
                    principles contained Truman Proclamation Sept. 28, 1945.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d40-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d40-f1-content">
                <p>The telegram was repeated to Jidda, London, and Cairo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d40-f2" n="2" xml:id="d40-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; this paragraph read as follows: “Most important consideration
                    believed to be issuance initial proclamation which follow most closely lines
                    Department general principles and in general pattern laid down after extensive
                    consultation of Department with various interested authorities and parties.”
                    (890.0145/5–1449)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d40-f3" n="3" xml:id="d40-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
